---
code: cli-strip-needs-path
when-fires: dorc strip was given no path. cli/lib.rs parse_args_from. No params - the invocation says everything.
why: 288 rul-dorc-strip-is-the-offramp: strip takes exactly one positional, so an empty one is unambiguous rather than a guess at intent.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- cli-strip-needs-path && mise run loom:promote -- cli-strip-needs-path`; prove it stuck with `mise run test`, which is also what catches anything else the promotion moved. `mise run loom:vars -- --all cli-strip-needs-path` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc strip
dorc: error[cli-strip-needs-path]: sm strip needs a file path
usage: dorc [probe|plan|apply] --book=<book.sh> [-o <oracle.sh>]... [--debug-argv]
